    outlook: "The future outlook suggests increased pressure on companies holding substantial crypto assets to enhance transparency and adopt more robust risk management protocols for their digital asset portfolios. Regulators globally, including those in India, are likely to leverage such incidents to bolster arguments for stricter oversight of cryptocurrency exchanges and custody providers. This will likely accelerate the growth of institutional-grade, regulated crypto custody services. For the broader crypto market, while short-term sentiment might experience minor fluctuations, the long-term trajectory points towards greater maturity, reinforced security measures, and clearer regulatory frameworks, albeit with persistent challenges from rogue entities and unregulated platforms.",
