    outlook: "The immediate outlook for Bitcoin remains influenced by the Federal Reserve\'s monetary policy. With a December rate hike appearing highly probable, Bitcoin could face continued short-term pressure as liquidity tightens and risk aversion prevails. However, the long-term outlook remains cautiously optimistic, driven by its fixed supply, upcoming halving event, and increasing mainstream acceptance. Investors will be closely watching subsequent Fed meetings for any shift in sentiment, as well as broader economic indicators and geopolitical stability. Bitcoin\'s ability to decouple from traditional markets in the future will depend on its evolving narrative and adoption rates.",
    conclusion: "Federal Reserve Governor Christopher Waller\'s comments have firmly anchored market expectations for a December interest rate hike, leading to a noticeable retreat in Bitcoin\'s price. This reaction underscores the significant influence of macroeconomic policy on the cryptocurrency market, highlighting its sensitivity to changes in global liquidity and risk appetite. While short-term pressures from a hawkish Fed are evident, Bitcoin\'s fundamental value proposition and long-term growth drivers, such as the halving and institutional adoption, continue to shape its broader trajectory. Investors should remain vigilant, balancing macro-economic headwinds with Bitcoin\'s unique characteristics and future potential.",
